:4,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I approve PKT-0017. The packet now delivers everything its goal asks for, which is what the last three reviews rejected it over.\n\n**Goal:** the bug-issue counts that were missing before are now in `baseline.md`. They come from the GitHub search API (`/search/issues`): per year for ONLYOFFICE and per month for Euro-Office. The fix-commit and crash-fix rates are given per year and per month, and the files and modules where fixes concentrate are listed. The script is in `.theseus/oracle/perf/defect-history.js`, and the matching rules that `baseline.md` quotes are the same regexes the script uses. That mismatch was a complaint in an earlier review and is now fixed.\n\n**Contract and budget:** no source code changed. The diff touches 4 files and adds about 200 lines, against limits of 6 files and 800 lines. The extra line in `.theseus/scoreboard/friction.jsonl` is outside `target.files`, but `AGENTS.md` requires that entry.\n\n**TEP-0004 checks:** the Executor log is filled in. The log says no follow-up was needed and `.theseus/spawn/` has no new request, which is consistent. This is an investigate packet, so the rule about keeping surprises in a test doesn't apply. The surprises themselves (the 1,828 rebase duplicates, issues being disabled on ONLYOFFICE/server, the search API's limit of five ORs, the two crash fixes missing from `main`) are all recorded in the log and in `baseline.md`.\n\n**Things that should be fixed later but don't justify a rejection:**\n- **Weak crash count for issues:** the crash/hang number is a plain text search for \"crash\", \"crashes\", \"hang\" or \"out of memory\", so it will include false positives. `baseline.md` states the query, so a reader can judge it.\n- **Loose crash rule for commits:** any commit subject containing \"crash\" counts as a crash fix, even if it isn't a fix. The script states this rule.\n- **Stale number in the log:** an earlier attempt's log line says ONLYOFFICE had 7 crash fixes in 2026 that are missing from Euro-Office. The recomputed table shows 2 crash fixes for ONLYOFFICE in 2026. That line should be marked as superseded.\n- **Atlas lessons not recorded:** the packet's \"Lessons for the Atlas\" section is empty. The `environment.md` lesson (only the per-repository API is blocked; `/search/issues` works) appears only in `friction.jsonl` and should go into the Atlas.\n- **Decision for the humans:** whether to port the fixes for bugs 81132 and 81576 to Euro-Office `main` is recorded in `baseline.md` for them to decide.\n\nVERDICT: APPROVE Goal fully met (fix-commit, crash and bug-issue rates plus hotspots, reproducible script), contract and budget respected","ttft_ms":2768,"type":"result","duration_ms":20186,"uuid":"c388e1e4-42f4-4972-a60c-399edae18b2b","ttft_stream_ms":1224,"time_to_request_ms":376,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":237,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":19,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":32,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":10,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":6,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":21,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":5,"request_build":10},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":49,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":183,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":217,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":141,"process_rss_mib_result":229,"process_anon_mib_result":139,"process_peak_rss_mib":266,"process_cpu_ms_turn":979,"process_wall_ms_turn":20185,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":381,"process_wall_ms_streaming":17159,"main_stream_count":4,"main_stream_event_count":278,"main_stream_chunk_count":87,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"artifact_opening_prefetch","slowest_producer_ms":7,"cpu_ms":21,"major_faults":0,"s